args: opentide --json deploy --help
exit: 0

━━━ stdout
Deploy rules to platform tenants

Usage: opentide deploy [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  migrate-state  Move vendor ids from rules into deployment state

Options:
      --platform <PLATFORM>
          Detection platform: sentinel, microsoft_defender, splunk, sentinel_one, crowdstrike, harfanglab, carbon_black_cloud, elastic, sysdig, bitdefender, graylog, exabeam, google_secops
          
          [possible values: sentinel, microsoft_defender, splunk, sentinel_one, crowdstrike, harfanglab, carbon_black_cloud, elastic, sysdig, bitdefender, graylog, exabeam, google_secops]

      --strategy <STRATEGY>
          Status strategy this run deploys (repeatable). PREVIEW: rules whose status maps to PREVIEW or UNIVERSAL. RELEASE: rules whose status maps to RELEASE or UNIVERSAL, and disables or deletes those mapping to DISABLEMENT or DELETION. Each rule goes to the tenants whose 'strategies' accept the run's strategy. Status names such as STAGING or PRODUCTION are not strategies

      --all
          Read every rule file, not only those the run changed (the pull or merge request, the push, or outside CI the last commit)

      --uuid <UUIDS>
          Read this rule (metadata.uuid) instead of the changed ones (repeatable). Cannot be combined with --all

      --file <FILES>
          Read this rule file, matched as by 'opentide validate --file', instead of the changed ones (repeatable). Cannot be combined with --all

      --wide
          Deploy the rule files read whatever their status strategy, INERT included

      --dry-run
          Print the plan and compile each rule; send nothing

      --keep-deprecated, --drop-deprecated
          Include rules whose status maps to DISABLEMENT or DELETION, so a RELEASE run disables or deletes them. Default: on, off with --all

      --skip-promotion
          Skip the status promotion of a RELEASE run on a push to the default branch

      --skip-unconfigured
          Exit 0 when every platform with rules to deploy has no [[tenants]] block

      --persist-state-externally
          Allow Defender, SentinelOne and CrowdStrike creates in a CI run other than a RELEASE run on a push; this pipeline must commit .opentide/states/deployment/ itself

      --prune
          With --strategy RELEASE: retire (delete) the rules deployed earlier whose rule file is gone: those the run's diff deleted, or with --all those deployment state records and no file holds. Without it, deploy only warns about them

      --help
          Print help

Examples:
  $ opentide deploy --strategy PREVIEW --all --dry-run
  $ opentide deploy --strategy RELEASE

━━━ stderr · empty
